stdout Circuit: bridge rectifier conduction loss and junction temperature (docs/thermal_and_protection.md sections 1 and 8).  br1 (+18v), br4 (+20v), br2 (+5v raw) and br5 (+12v power) are discrete bridges of four st stps20m100s 100 v / 20 a d2pak schottky diodes (ds6169 rev 5) since the 2026-09-07 review; br3 (+50v) stays a gbpc3510w block under a boyd 6224bg basket (9.4 c/w). each rail is rectified with the real winding, the diode model and its filter, then loaded with (a) the sustained design load, (b) the everything-on / fuse-limit load. per case: dc output current (average of |i_leg|), leg rms current, the model dissipation of the whole bridge (ac-side minus dc-side power) and, for the schottky bridges, the per-diode loss from the datasheet equation p = 0.425 if(av) + 0.0088 if(rms)^2 with if(av) = iavg/2 and if(rms) = irms/sqrt(2) (each diode conducts every other half-cycle), the required rth(j-a) for tj <= 110 c at 50 c ambient and the tj on the copper area assumed per diode (st figure 9, d2pak on 35 um fr4: 70 / 55 / 46 / 39 / 35 / 31 / 30 c/w at 0.5 / 1 / 2 / 5 / 10 / 20 / 40 cm2; 2 oz outer copper taken as 10 % better): br1 diodes 15 cm2 each (33 c/w x 0.9 = 29.7 c/w; the 2.5 ohm all-lamps load draws 6.4 a from the higher schottky rail), br4 4 cm2 (36 c/w), br2 / br5 2 cm2 (41 c/w). br3: p = 2 (0.80 iavg + 0.017 irms^2) (gbpc35 max vf), rth(j-a) = 1.4 + 0.5 + 9.4 x 1.05 = 11.8 c/w, tj <= 125 c
